IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- PART 11 -- Miscellaneous Provisions (regulations 101 to 110 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist
-- Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017, S.I. 2017/692,
-- United Kingdom), lines 2854-2955 of uksi-2017-692.txt.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.  The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER.  A decision function answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING.
-- JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words; each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (...)` with the quoted words.  NOTHING is "the text does not answer"; each such
-- branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Marginal readings, listed in NOTES.md: (a) a trailing "if" on a power, an "is"-definition,
-- an "except" and a flat negative are the text's no; (b) a grant or a prohibition limited by its
-- own wording is not a no; (c) a "must" that has not been done is the text's no.
-- Rulings of 2026-11-05, tagged `[ruled 2026-11-05 (a) period]` and `[ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]`
-- on the branch (they are not the marginal readings above): a period the text fixes in its own
-- words answers JUST FALSE outside it; a "where" condition that is not met answers JUST FALSE;
-- a scope limit with no "only" answers NOTHING outside the scope.
-- A duty function (a "must") answers JUST FALSE only for a breach.  Where the duty arises "if" or
-- "where" something holds, a companion function, `... the duty ... arises`, answers JUST FALSE when
-- it does not arise, and the duty function answers NOTHING then.
-- A seam is marked `-- SEAM S-n (asking|answering)`.

§ `Part 11 -- Miscellaneous Provisions`

§§ `Regulation 101 -- Recovery of charges and penalties through the court`

-- Reg 101: a charge or penalty imposed on a relevant person or a payment service provider by the FCA or the Commissioners is a debt due from that person to the body that imposed it ("respectively"), and is recoverable accordingly.  A penalty on an officer under regulation 76(3) is imposed on neither kind of person, so it is not here.
-- src:2856 | Any charge or penalty imposed on a relevant person or on a payment service provider by the FCA or the Commissioners under these Regulations is a debt due from that person to the FCA or the Commissioners respectively, and is recoverable accordingly.
@ref reg 101 (src:2856)
GIVEN `the charge or penalty is imposed on a relevant person or on a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body that imposes it` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE Authority
DECIDE `reg 101 the charge or penalty is a debt due to` IS
    IF     `the charge or penalty is imposed on a relevant person or on a payment service provider`
       AND (   `the body that imposes it` EQUALS `the Financial Conduct Authority`
            OR `the body that imposes it` EQUALS `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`)
    THEN JUST `the body that imposes it`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any charge or penalty imposed on a relevant person or on a payment service provider by the FCA or the Commissioners"

§§ `Regulation 102 -- Costs of supervision`

-- Reg 102(1): the FCA and the Commissioners may impose charges on five classes of person.
-- src:2858 | (1) The FCA and the Commissioners may impose charges on—
-- src:2859 | (a) applicants for approval under Chapter 3 of Part 2;
-- src:2860 | (b) applicants for registration under Chapter 2 of Part 6;
-- src:2861 | (c) relevant persons supervised by them;
-- src:2862 | (d) payment service providers supervised by them;
-- src:2863 | (e) professional bodies listed in Schedule 1, for which they undertake enforcement action in relation to relevant persons supervised by those professional bodies.
@ref reg 102(1) (src:2858-2863)
DECLARE `reg 102(1) class` IS ONE OF
    `reg 102(1)(a) applicants for approval under Chapter 3 of Part 2`
    `reg 102(1)(b) applicants for registration under Chapter 2 of Part 6`
    `reg 102(1)(c) relevant persons supervised by them`
    `reg 102(1)(d) payment service providers supervised by them`
    `reg 102(1)(e) professional bodies listed in Schedule 1, for which they undertake enforcement action in relation to relevant persons supervised by those professional bodies`
    `reg 102(1) some other class`

@ref reg 102(1) (src:2858-2863)
GIVEN `the charge is imposed by the FCA or the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
      what IS A `reg 102(1) class`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 102(1) the charge may be imposed on` IS
    IF `the charge is imposed by the FCA or the Commissioners`
    THEN CONSIDER what
         WHEN `reg 102(1)(a) applicants for approval under Chapter 3 of Part 2` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 102(1)(b) applicants for registration under Chapter 2 of Part 6` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 102(1)(c) relevant persons supervised by them` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 102(1)(d) payment service providers supervised by them` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 102(1)(e) professional bodies listed in Schedule 1, for which they undertake enforcement action in relation to relevant persons supervised by those professional bodies` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 102(1) some other class` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the items are listed and the text does not say others are barred
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for the FCA and the Commissioners

-- Reg 102(2): charges must not exceed what the body considers will enable it to meet its reasonably incurred expenses.  A charge at or below the figure is not made lawful by this paragraph (it is the paragraph (1) power that makes it so).
-- src:2864 | (2) Charges levied under paragraph (1) must not exceed such amount as the FCA or the Commissioners (as the case may be) consider will enable them to meet any expenses reasonably incurred by them in carrying out their functions under these Regulations or for any incidental purpose (including any expenses reasonably incurred by them in undertaking enforcement action on behalf of a self-regulatory organisation).
@ref reg 102(2) (src:2864)
GIVEN `the charge levied under paragraph (1), in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount the FCA or the Commissioners consider will enable them to meet the expenses reasonably incurred in carrying out their functions under these Regulations or for any incidental purpose, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 102(2) the charge is permitted` IS
    IF `the charge levied under paragraph (1), in pounds` > `the amount the FCA or the Commissioners consider will enable them to meet the expenses reasonably incurred in carrying out their functions under these Regulations or for any incidental purpose, in pounds`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Charges levied under paragraph (1) must not exceed such amount as the FCA or the Commissioners (as the case may be) consider will enable them to meet any expenses reasonably incurred by them" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a charge that does not exceed the amount is not made lawful by this paragraph

-- Reg 102(3): "without prejudice to the generality of paragraph (2)": a charge may be levied in respect of each of the premises.
-- src:2865 | (3) Without prejudice to the generality of paragraph (2), a charge may be levied in respect of each of the premises at which the relevant person, the provider or a person connected with the relevant person or the provider carries on (or proposes to carry on) business or professional activities.
@ref reg 102(3) (src:2865)
GIVEN `the premises are premises at which the relevant person, the provider or a person connected with the relevant person or the provider carries on, or proposes to carry on, business or professional activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 102(3) a charge may be levied in respect of each of the premises` IS
    IF `the premises are premises at which the relevant person, the provider or a person connected with the relevant person or the provider carries on, or proposes to carry on, business or professional activities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Without prejudice to the generality of paragraph (2)"

-- Reg 102(4): the FCA pays to the Treasury, for each financial year, the amounts it received that year by way of penalties under Part 9.
-- src:2866 | (4) The FCA must in respect of each of its financial years pay to the Treasury any amounts received by the FCA during the year by way of penalties imposed under Part 9.
@ref reg 102(4) (src:2866)
GIVEN `the amount the FCA received during the financial year by way of penalties imposed under Part 9, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount the FCA paid to the Treasury in respect of that year, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 102(4) the FCA paid the penalties it received to the Treasury` IS
    IF `the amount the FCA received during the financial year by way of penalties imposed under Part 9, in pounds` > 0
    THEN IF `the amount the FCA paid to the Treasury in respect of that year, in pounds` >= `the amount the FCA received during the financial year by way of penalties imposed under Part 9, in pounds`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The FCA must in respect of each of its financial years pay to the Treasury any amounts received by the FCA during the year by way of penalties imposed under Part 9" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any amounts received": a year in which nothing was received is not covered

-- Reg 102(5): the Treasury may give directions to the FCA on how to comply with the duty in paragraph (4).
-- src:2867 | (5) The Treasury may give directions to the FCA as to how the FCA is to comply with the duty under paragraph (4).
@ref reg 102(5) (src:2867)
GIVEN `the directions are as to how the FCA is to comply with the duty under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 102(5) the Treasury may give directions to the FCA` IS
    IF `the directions are as to how the FCA is to comply with the duty under paragraph (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as to how the FCA is to comply with the duty under paragraph (4)"

-- Reg 102(6): the directions may in particular specify the time of payment and require information at specified times.  "In particular": not closed.
-- src:2868 | (6) The directions may in particular—
-- src:2869 | (a) specify the time when any payment is required to be made to the Treasury; and
-- src:2870 | (b) require the FCA to provide the Treasury at specified times with information relating to penalties that the FCA has imposed under Part 9.
@ref reg 102(6) (src:2868-2870)
DECLARE `reg 102(6) content` IS ONE OF
    `reg 102(6)(a) specify the time when any payment is required to be made to the Treasury`
    `reg 102(6)(b) require the FCA to provide the Treasury at specified times with information relating to penalties that the FCA has imposed under Part 9`
    `reg 102(6) some other content`

@ref reg 102(6) (src:2868-2870)
GIVEN `the directions are given under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      what IS A `reg 102(6) content`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 102(6) the directions may` IS
    IF `the directions are given under paragraph (5)`
    THEN CONSIDER what
         WHEN `reg 102(6)(a) specify the time when any payment is required to be made to the Treasury` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 102(6)(b) require the FCA to provide the Treasury at specified times with information relating to penalties that the FCA has imposed under Part 9` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 102(6) some other content` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "in particular" does not close the list
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of directions under paragraph (5)

-- Reg 102(7): the Treasury pays into the Consolidated Fund any sums received under this regulation.
-- src:2871 | (7) The Treasury must pay into the Consolidated Fund any sums received by them under this regulation.
@ref reg 102(7) (src:2871)
GIVEN `the Treasury received sums under this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Treasury paid the sums into the Consolidated Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 102(7) the Treasury paid the sums into the Consolidated Fund` IS
    IF `the Treasury received sums under this regulation`
    THEN IF `the Treasury paid the sums into the Consolidated Fund`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Treasury must pay into the Consolidated Fund any sums received by them under this regulation" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- Reg 102(8): in paragraph (2) "expenses" includes expenses incurred by a local weights and measures authority or the Department for the Economy under arrangements with the FCA or the Commissioners.
-- src:2872 | (8) In paragraph (2), “expenses” includes expenses incurred by a local weights and measures authority or the Department for the Economy pursuant to arrangements made for the purposes of these Regulations with the FCA or with the Commissioners—
-- src:2873 | (a) by or on behalf of the authority; or
-- src:2874 | (b) by the Department for the Economy.
@ref reg 102(8) (src:2872-2874)
GIVEN `the expenses were incurred by or on behalf of a local weights and measures authority, or by the Department for the Economy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were incurred pursuant to arrangements made for the purposes of these Regulations with the FCA or with the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 102(8) the expenses are expenses within paragraph (2)` IS
    IF `the expenses were incurred by or on behalf of a local weights and measures authority, or by the Department for the Economy` AND `they were incurred pursuant to arrangements made for the purposes of these Regulations with the FCA or with the Commissioners`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“expenses” includes"

§§ `Regulation 103 -- Obligations on public authorities`

-- Reg 103(1): the twenty-one bodies and persons that must inform the NCA if they know or suspect, or have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing.  Several limbs name the capacity in which the body must act (limbs (l), (m)); the capacity is part of the constructor.
-- src:2876 | (1) The following bodies and persons must, if they know or suspect or have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing, as soon as practicable, inform the NCA—
-- src:2877 | (a) the Auditor General for Scotland;
-- src:2878 | (b) the Auditor General for Wales;
-- src:2879 | (c) the Bank of England;
-- src:2880 | (d) the Comptroller and Auditor General;
-- src:2881 | (e) the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland;
-- src:2882 | (f) the FCA;
-- src:2883 | (g) the Gambling Commission;
-- src:2884 | (h) the Official Solicitor to the Supreme Court;
-- src:2885 | (i) the Pensions Regulator;
-- src:2886 | (j) the PRA;
-- src:2887 | (k) the Public Trustee;
-- src:2888 | (l) the Secretary of State, in the exercise of his or her functions under enactments relating to companies and insolvency;
-- src:2889 | (m) the Treasury, in the exercise of their functions under FSMA;
-- src:2890 | (n) the Treasury Solicitor;
-- src:2891 | (o) a designated professional body for the purposes of Part 20 of FSMA (provision of financial services by members of the professions);
-- src:2892 | (p) a person or inspector appointed under section 65 (investigations on behalf of FCA) or 66 (inspections and special meetings) of the Friendly Societies Act 1992 ;
-- src:2893 | (q) an inspector appointed under section 106 of the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies 2014 (appointment of inspectors) or section 18 of the Credit Unions Act 1979 (power to appoint inspector);
-- src:2894 | (r) an inspector appointed under section 431 (investigation of a company on its own application), 432 (other company investigations), 442 (power to investigate company ownership) or 446D (appointment of replacement inspectors) of the Companies Act 1985 ;
-- src:2895 | (s) a person or inspector appointed under section 55 (investigations on behalf of FCA) or 56 (inspections and special meetings) of the Building Societies Act 1986 ;
-- src:2896 | (t) a person appointed under section 167 (appointment of persons to carry out investigations), 168(3) or (5) (appointment of persons to carry out investigations in particular cases), 169(1)(b) (investigations to support overseas regulator) or 284 (power to investigate affairs of a scheme) of FSMA , or under regulations made under section 262(2)(k) (open-ended investment companies) of that Act , to conduct an investigation; and
-- src:2897 | (u) a person authorised to require the production of documents under section 447 (Secretary of State's power to require production of documents) of the Companies Act 1985 , or section 84 of the Companies Act 1989 (exercise of powers by officer).
@ref reg 103(1) (src:2876-2897)
DECLARE `reg 103(1) body` IS ONE OF
    `reg 103(1)(a) the Auditor General for Scotland`
    `reg 103(1)(b) the Auditor General for Wales`
    `reg 103(1)(c) the Bank of England`
    `reg 103(1)(d) the Comptroller and Auditor General`
    `reg 103(1)(e) the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland`
    `reg 103(1)(f) the FCA`
    `reg 103(1)(g) the Gambling Commission`
    `reg 103(1)(h) the Official Solicitor to the Supreme Court`
    `reg 103(1)(i) the Pensions Regulator`
    `reg 103(1)(j) the PRA`
    `reg 103(1)(k) the Public Trustee`
    `reg 103(1)(l) the Secretary of State, in the exercise of his or her functions under enactments relating to companies and insolvency`
    `reg 103(1)(m) the Treasury, in the exercise of their functions under FSMA`
    `reg 103(1)(n) the Treasury Solicitor`
    `reg 103(1)(o) a designated professional body for the purposes of Part 20 of FSMA`
    `reg 103(1)(p) a person or inspector appointed under section 65 or 66 of the Friendly Societies Act 1992`
    `reg 103(1)(q) an inspector appointed under section 106 of the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies 2014 or section 18 of the Credit Unions Act 1979`
    `reg 103(1)(r) an inspector appointed under section 431, 432, 442 or 446D of the Companies Act 1985`
    `reg 103(1)(s) a person or inspector appointed under section 55 or 56 of the Building Societies Act 1986`
    `reg 103(1)(t) a person appointed under section 167, 168(3) or (5), 169(1)(b) or 284 of FSMA, or under regulations made under section 262(2)(k) of that Act, to conduct an investigation`
    `reg 103(1)(u) a person authorised to require the production of documents under section 447 of the Companies Act 1985, or section 84 of the Companies Act 1989`
    `reg 103(1) some other body`

@ref reg 103(1) (src:2876-2897)
GIVEN who IS A `reg 103(1) body`
      `the body or person knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 103(1) the duty to inform the NCA arises` IS
    IF who EQUALS `reg 103(1) some other body`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): twenty-one bodies and persons are listed and the paragraph does not say that no other must inform the NCA
    ELSE IF `the body or person knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, if they know or suspect or have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing" [marginal (a)]

@ref reg 103(1) (src:2876-2897)
GIVEN who IS A `reg 103(1) body`
      `the body or person knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body or person informed the NCA as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 103(1) the body or person informed the NCA as required` IS
    IF who EQUALS `reg 103(1) some other body`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): twenty-one bodies and persons are listed and the paragraph does not say that no other must inform the NCA
    ELSE IF `the body or person knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing`
         THEN IF `the body or person informed the NCA as soon as practicable`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, if they know or suspect or have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing, as soon as practicable, inform the NCA" [marginal (c)]
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise, so there is no answer here: ask `reg 103(1) the duty to inform the NCA arises` ("if they know or suspect or have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting")

-- Reg 103(2): a disclosure under paragraph (1) is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information.
-- src:2898 | (2) A disclosure made under paragraph (1) is not to be taken to breach any restriction, however imposed, on the disclosure of information.
@ref reg 103(2) (src:2898)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 103(2) the disclosure breaches a restriction on the disclosure of information` IS
    IF `the disclosure is made under paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A disclosure made under paragraph (1) is not to be taken to breach any restriction, however imposed, on the disclosure of information" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- Reg 103(3): no civil liability for a disclosure under paragraph (1) made in good faith.
-- src:2899 | (3) Where a disclosure under paragraph (1) is made in good faith, no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person by whom, or on whose behalf, it is made.
@ref reg 103(3) (src:2899)
GIVEN `the disclosure under paragraph (1) is made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 103(3) civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure` IS
    IF `the disclosure under paragraph (1) is made in good faith`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person by whom, or on whose behalf, it is made" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a disclosure under paragraph (1) is made in good faith"

§§ `Regulation 104 -- Suspicious activity disclosures`

-- Reg 104(4): "suspicious activity disclosure" (the definition behind regulation 66(9)).
-- src:2904 | (4) In this regulation, a “suspicious activity disclosure” is a disclosure made to the NCA under—
-- src:2905 | (a) Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 (terrorist property) ;
-- src:2906 | (b) Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (money laundering) .
@ref reg 104(4) (src:2904-2906)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made to the NCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made under Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 (terrorist property)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made under Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (money laundering)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 104(4) the disclosure is a suspicious activity disclosure` IS
    IF `the disclosure is made to the NCA` AND (`it is made under Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 (terrorist property)` OR `it is made under Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (money laundering)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “suspicious activity disclosure” is a disclosure made to the NCA under— (a) Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 (terrorist property); (b) Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (money laundering)" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 104(1): the NCA must make arrangements to provide appropriate feedback at least once a year.
-- src:2901 | (1) The NCA must make arrangements to provide appropriate feedback on the suspicious activity disclosures it has received at least once a year.
@ref reg 104(1) (src:2901)
GIVEN `the number of times in the year the NCA made arrangements to provide feedback on the suspicious activity disclosures it has received` IS A NUMBER
      `the feedback is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 104(1) the NCA made arrangements to provide appropriate feedback` IS
    IF TRUE
    THEN IF `the number of times in the year the NCA made arrangements to provide feedback on the suspicious activity disclosures it has received` >= 1 AND `the feedback is appropriate`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The NCA must make arrangements to provide appropriate feedback on the suspicious activity disclosures it has received at least once a year" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- Reg 104(2): the feedback may be provided by the NCA jointly with another person, or by another person on its behalf.
-- src:2902 | (2) The feedback referred to in paragraph (1) may be provided by the NCA jointly with another person, or by another person on behalf of the NCA.
@ref reg 104(2) (src:2902)
GIVEN `the NCA provides it jointly with another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another person provides it on behalf of the NCA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 104(2) the feedback may be provided in the way` IS
    IF `the NCA provides it jointly with another person` OR `another person provides it on behalf of the NCA`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "jointly with another person, or by another person on behalf of the NCA"

-- Reg 104(3): in any form the NCA thinks fit.
-- src:2903 | (3) The feedback referred to in paragraph (1) may be provided in any form the NCA thinks fit.
@ref reg 104(3) (src:2903)
GIVEN `the form is one the NCA thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 104(3) the feedback may be provided in the form` IS
    IF `the form is one the NCA thinks fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any form the NCA thinks fit"

-- Reg 104A: Schedule 6A makes provision in relation to the NCA as the United Kingdom's financial intelligence unit; a pointer to the part that owns the Schedule.
-- src:2908 | Schedule 6A makes provision in relation to the NCA in its capacity as the United Kingdom’s financial intelligence unit.
