GIVETH A STRING
`reg 104A the provision in relation to the NCA as the United Kingdom's financial intelligence unit is made by` MEANS "Schedule 6A"

§§ `Regulation 105 -- Disclosure by the Commissioners`

-- Reg 105(1): the Commissioners may disclose information to the FCA if the disclosure is for the purpose of enabling or assisting the FCA to discharge its functions under the Payment Services Regulations 2017 or the Electronic Money Regulations 2011.  A trailing "if": marginal reading (a).
-- src:2910 | (1) The Commissioners may disclose to the FCA information held in connection with their functions under these Regulations if the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting the FCA to discharge any of its functions under the Payment Services Regulations 2017 or the Electronic Money Regulations 2011 .
@ref reg 105(1) (src:2910)
GIVEN `the information is held in connection with the Commissioners' functions under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting the FCA to discharge any of its functions under the Payment Services Regulations 2017 or the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 105(1) the Commissioners may disclose the information to the FCA` IS
    IF `the information is held in connection with the Commissioners' functions under these Regulations` AND `the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting the FCA to discharge any of its functions under the Payment Services Regulations 2017 or the Electronic Money Regulations 2011`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commissioners may disclose to the FCA information held in connection with their functions under these Regulations if the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting the FCA to discharge any of its functions" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 105(2): information so disclosed may not be disclosed by the FCA or by anyone who receives it from the FCA, except in four cases.  JUST TRUE: the bar applies to this disclosure.  JUST FALSE: an exception takes it outside the bar.  The prohibition on each bearer the text names (the FCA; any person who receives the information) is derived below (ruling N2).
-- src:2911 | (2) Information disclosed to the FCA under paragraph (1) may not be disclosed by the FCA or any person who receives the information directly or indirectly from the FCA except—
-- src:2912 | (a) to, or in accordance with authority given by, the Commissioners;
-- src:2913 | (b) with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, any criminal proceedings;
-- src:2914 | (c) with a view to the institution of any other proceedings by the FCA, for the purposes of any such proceedings, or for the purposes of any reference to the Upper Tribunal under the Payment Services Regulations 2017; or
-- src:2915 | (d) in the form of a summary or collection of information so framed as not to enable information relating to any particular person to be ascertained from it.
@ref reg 105(2) (src:2911-2915)
GIVEN `the information was disclosed to the FCA under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to, or in accordance with authority given by, the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, any criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is with a view to the institution of any other proceedings by the FCA, for the purposes of any such proceedings, or for the purposes of any reference to the Upper Tribunal under the Payment Services Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is in the form of a summary or collection of information so framed as not to enable information relating to any particular person to be ascertained from it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 105(2) the FCA or a recipient must not disclose the information` IS
    IF NOT `the information was disclosed to the FCA under paragraph (1)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Information disclosed to the FCA under paragraph (1)"
    ELSE IF     `the disclosure is to, or in accordance with authority given by, the Commissioners`
             OR `the disclosure is with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, any criminal proceedings`
             OR `the disclosure is with a view to the institution of any other proceedings by the FCA, for the purposes of any such proceedings, or for the purposes of any reference to the Upper Tribunal under the Payment Services Regulations 2017`
             OR `the disclosure is in the form of a summary or collection of information so framed as not to enable information relating to any particular person to be ascertained from it`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be disclosed by the FCA or any person who receives the information directly or indirectly from the FCA except—": the four exceptions take the disclosure outside the bar [marginal (a)]
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `reg 105(2) FCA party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 105(2) the FCA`

DECLARE `reg 105(2) FCA action` IS ONE OF
    `reg 105(2) the FCA discloses the information`

@ref reg 105(2) (src:2911-2915)
GIVEN `reg 105(2) the FCA or a recipient must not disclose the information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 105(2) FCA party` `reg 105(2) FCA action`
DECIDE `reg 105(2) FCA the prohibition on the FCA` IS
    IF `reg 105(2) the FCA or a recipient must not disclose the information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `reg 105(2) the FCA`
         SHANT `reg 105(2) the FCA discloses the information`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `reg 105(2) the FCA` BECAUSE "the FCA disclosed information received under regulation 105(1) in a way that none of the four exceptions in regulation 105(2) covers"
    ELSE FULFILLED

DECLARE `reg 105(2) recipient party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 105(2) a person who receives the information from the FCA`

DECLARE `reg 105(2) recipient action` IS ONE OF
    `reg 105(2) the person discloses the information`

@ref reg 105(2) (src:2911-2915)
GIVEN `reg 105(2) the FCA or a recipient must not disclose the information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 105(2) recipient party` `reg 105(2) recipient action`
DECIDE `reg 105(2) recipient the prohibition on a person who receives the information from the FCA` IS
    IF `reg 105(2) the FCA or a recipient must not disclose the information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `reg 105(2) a person who receives the information from the FCA`
         SHANT `reg 105(2) the person discloses the information`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `reg 105(2) a person who receives the information from the FCA` BECAUSE "a person who received information from the FCA disclosed it in a way that none of the four exceptions in regulation 105(2) covers"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `Regulation 106 -- General restrictions`

-- Reg 106: these Regulations do not authorise or require a disclosure that contravenes the data protection legislation or is prohibited by the Investigatory Powers Act 2016.  No bearer is named, so no prohibition is derived.
-- src:2917 | These Regulations do not authorise or require—
-- src:2918 | (a) a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation; or
-- src:2919 | (b) a disclosure which is prohibited by any of Parts 1 to 3 or 5 to 7 of the Investigatory Powers Act 2016 .
@ref reg 106 (src:2917-2919)
GIVEN `the disclosure would be in contravention of the data protection legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is prohibited by any of Parts 1 to 3 or 5 to 7 of the Investigatory Powers Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 106 these Regulations authorise or require the disclosure` IS
    IF `the disclosure would be in contravention of the data protection legislation` OR `the disclosure is prohibited by any of Parts 1 to 3 or 5 to 7 of the Investigatory Powers Act 2016`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "These Regulations do not authorise or require— (a) a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation; or (b) a disclosure which is prohibited by any of Parts 1 to 3 or 5 to 7 of the Investigatory Powers Act 2016" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `Regulation 107 -- Transfers between the United Kingdom and the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man`

-- Reg 107: in determining whether a person has failed to comply with a requirement in the funds transfer regulation, a transfer between the United Kingdom and the Channel Islands or the Isle of Man is treated as a transfer within the United Kingdom.
-- src:2921 | In determining whether a person has failed to comply with any requirement in the funds transfer regulation, any transfer of funds between the United Kingdom and—
-- src:2922 | (a) the Channel Islands; or
-- src:2923 | (b) the Isle of Man;
-- src:2924 | is to be treated as a transfer of funds within the United Kingdom.
@ref reg 107 (src:2921-2924)
DECLARE `reg 107 place` IS ONE OF
    `reg 107(a) the Channel Islands`
    `reg 107(b) the Isle of Man`
    `reg 107 some other place`

@ref reg 107 (src:2921-2924)
GIVEN `a person's compliance with a requirement in the funds transfer regulation is being determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place at the other end of the transfer from the United Kingdom` IS A `reg 107 place`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 107 the transfer is treated as a transfer of funds within the United Kingdom` IS
    IF `a person's compliance with a requirement in the funds transfer regulation is being determined`
    THEN CONSIDER `the place at the other end of the transfer from the United Kingdom`
         WHEN `reg 107(a) the Channel Islands` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 107(b) the Isle of Man` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 107 some other place` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the regulation treats transfers with the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man this way and says nothing of any other place
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining whether a person has failed to comply with any requirement in the funds transfer regulation"

§§ `Regulation 108 -- Review`

-- Reg 108(1): the Treasury must from time to time carry out a review of the regulatory provision in these Regulations and publish a report of its conclusions.
-- src:2926 | (1) The Treasury must from time to time—
-- src:2927 | (a) carry out a review of the regulatory provision contained in these Regulations; and
-- src:2928 | (b) publish a report setting out the conclusions of the review.
@ref reg 108(1) (src:2926-2928)
GIVEN `the Treasury carried out a review of the regulatory provision contained in these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Treasury published a report setting out the conclusions of the review` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 108(1) the Treasury carried out a review and published a report` IS
    IF TRUE
    THEN IF `the Treasury carried out a review of the regulatory provision contained in these Regulations` AND `the Treasury published a report setting out the conclusions of the review`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Treasury must from time to time— (a) carry out a review of the regulatory provision contained in these Regulations; and (b) publish a report setting out the conclusions of the review" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- Reg 108(2): the first report must be published before 26th June 2022.  A report published on 26 June 2022 is not before it.
-- src:2929 | (2) The first report must be published before 26th June 2022.
@ref reg 108(2) (src:2929)
GIVEN `the date the first report was published` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 108(2) the first report was published in time` IS
    IF `the date the first report was published` < Date 26 6 2022
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first report must be published before 26th June 2022" [marginal (c)]

-- Reg 108(3): subsequent reports at intervals not exceeding 5 years.  The interval is in years.
-- src:2930 | (3) Subsequent reports must be published at intervals not exceeding 5 years.
@ref reg 108(3) (src:2930)
GIVEN `the report is a subsequent report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the years between the publication of the earlier report and this one` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 108(3) the subsequent report was published in time` IS
    IF `the report is a subsequent report`
    THEN IF `the years between the publication of the earlier report and this one` <= 5
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsequent reports must be published at intervals not exceeding 5 years" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- Reg 108(4): section 30(3) of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 requires the review to have regard, so far as reasonable, to how three instruments are implemented in other member States.  Whether a review did so is a plain input per limb.
-- src:2931 | (4) Section 30(3) of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 (provision for review) requires that a review carried out under this regulation must, so far as is reasonable, have regard to how—
-- src:2932 | (a) the emission allowance auctioning regulation;
-- src:2933 | (b) the fourth money laundering directive; and
-- src:2934 | (c) the funds transfer regulation;
-- src:2935 | are implemented in other member States.
@ref reg 108(4) (src:2931-2935)
GIVEN `the review is carried out under this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the review had regard, so far as reasonable, to how the emission allowance auctioning regulation is implemented in other member States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the review had regard, so far as reasonable, to how the fourth money laundering directive is implemented in other member States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the review had regard, so far as reasonable, to how the funds transfer regulation is implemented in other member States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 108(4) the review had regard to how the instruments are implemented in other member States` IS
    IF `the review is carried out under this regulation`
    THEN IF `the review had regard, so far as reasonable, to how the emission allowance auctioning regulation is implemented in other member States` AND `the review had regard, so far as reasonable, to how the fourth money laundering directive is implemented in other member States` AND `the review had regard, so far as reasonable, to how the funds transfer regulation is implemented in other member States`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a review carried out under this regulation must, so far as is reasonable, have regard to how— (a) the emission allowance auctioning regulation; (b) the fourth money laundering directive; and (c) the funds transfer regulation; are implemented in other member States" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- Reg 108(5): section 30(4) of that Act requires the report to set out four things.
-- src:2936 | (5) Section 30(4) of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 requires that a report published under this regulation must, in particular—
-- src:2937 | (a) set out the objectives intended to be achieved by the regulatory provision referred to in paragraph (1)(a);
-- src:2938 | (b) assess the extent to which those objectives are achieved;
-- src:2939 | (c) assess whether those objectives remain appropriate; and
-- src:2940 | (d) if those objectives remain appropriate, assess the extent to which they could be achieved in another way which involves less onerous regulatory provision.
@ref reg 108(5) (src:2936-2940)
GIVEN `the report is published under this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the objectives intended to be achieved by the regulatory provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it assesses the extent to which those objectives are achieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it assesses whether those objectives remain appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those objectives remain appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it assesses the extent to which they could be achieved in another way which involves less onerous regulatory provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 108(5) the report sets out what it must` IS
    IF `the report is published under this regulation`
    THEN IF `it sets out the objectives intended to be achieved by the regulatory provision` AND `it assesses the extent to which those objectives are achieved` AND `it assesses whether those objectives remain appropriate` AND ((NOT `those objectives remain appropriate`) OR `it assesses the extent to which they could be achieved in another way which involves less onerous regulatory provision`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a report published under this regulation must, in particular— (a) set out the objectives ...; (b) assess the extent to which those objectives are achieved; (c) assess whether those objectives remain appropriate; and (d) if those objectives remain appropriate, assess the extent to which they could be achieved in another way" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- Reg 108(6): "regulatory provision" has the meaning given by sections 28 to 32 of that Act; a pointer.
-- src:2941 | (6) In this regulation, “regulatory provision” has the same meaning as in sections 28 to 32 of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 (see section 32 of that Act).
@ref reg 108(6) (src:2941)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 108(6) regulatory provision is given by` MEANS "sections 28 to 32 of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 (see section 32 of that Act)"

§§ `Regulation 109 -- Consequential amendments`

-- Reg 109: Schedule 7 makes amendments relating to these Regulations; a pointer to the Schedule, which the part that owns it encodes.
-- src:2943 | Schedule 7 makes amendments relating to these Regulations.
@ref reg 109 (src:2943)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 109 the amendments relating to these Regulations are made by` MEANS "Schedule 7"

§§ `Regulation 110 -- Revocation and saving provisions`

-- Reg 110(5) and (6): which instruments are the "old money laundering regulations" and the "old transfer of funds regulations".  Both definitions say "means", so any other instrument is not one.
-- src:2949 | (5) The “old money laundering regulations” means—
-- src:2950 | (a) the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 ;
-- src:2951 | (b) the Money Laundering (Amendment) Regulations 2007 ;
-- src:2952 | (c) the Money Laundering (Amendment) Regulations 2011 ;
-- src:2953 | (d) the Money Laundering (Amendment) Regulations 2012 ; and
-- src:2954 | (e) the Money Laundering (Amendment) Regulations 2015 .
-- src:2955 | (6) The “old transfer of funds regulations” means the Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2007 .
@ref reg 110(5) (src:2949-2955)
DECLARE `reg 110 instrument` IS ONE OF
    `reg 110(5)(a) the Money Laundering Regulations 2007`
    `reg 110(5)(b) the Money Laundering (Amendment) Regulations 2007`
    `reg 110(5)(c) the Money Laundering (Amendment) Regulations 2011`
    `reg 110(5)(d) the Money Laundering (Amendment) Regulations 2012`
    `reg 110(5)(e) the Money Laundering (Amendment) Regulations 2015`
    `reg 110(6) the Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2007`
    `reg 110 some other instrument`

@ref reg 110(5) (src:2949-2954)
GIVEN instrument IS A `reg 110 instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 110(5) the instrument is one of the old money laundering regulations` IS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `reg 110(5)(a) the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 110(5)(b) the Money Laundering (Amendment) Regulations 2007` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 110(5)(c) the Money Laundering (Amendment) Regulations 2011` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 110(5)(d) the Money Laundering (Amendment) Regulations 2012` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 110(5)(e) the Money Laundering (Amendment) Regulations 2015` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 110(6) the Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2007` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The “old money laundering regulations” means—" the five listed instruments [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 110 some other instrument` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The “old money laundering regulations” means—" the five listed instruments [marginal (a)]

@ref reg 110(6) (src:2955)
GIVEN instrument IS A `reg 110 instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 110(6) the instrument is the old transfer of funds regulations` IS
    IF instrument EQUALS `reg 110(6) the Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2007`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The “old transfer of funds regulations” means the Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2007" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 110(1): the old regulations are revoked.
-- src:2945 | (1) The old money laundering regulations and the old transfer of funds regulations are revoked.
@ref reg 110(1) (src:2945)
GIVEN `the instrument is one of the old money laundering regulations or the old transfer of funds regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 110(1) the instrument is revoked` IS
    IF `the instrument is one of the old money laundering regulations or the old transfer of funds regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The old money laundering regulations and the old transfer of funds regulations are revoked"

-- Reg 110(2): the old regulations continue to have effect where the conduct constituting a contravention or an offence began before the day these Regulations came into force (26 June 2017, in the core).  Conduct that began on that day is not before it, and conduct that began on or after it is outside the "where" clause, so the answer is JUST FALSE (ruled 2026-11-05, (b)).
-- src:2946 | (2) The old money laundering regulations and the old transfer of funds regulations shall continue to have effect where the conduct constituting a contravention of one of those Regulations, or an offence under one of those Regulations began before the date on which these Regulations come into force.
@ref reg 110(2) (src:2946)
GIVEN `the day the conduct constituting the contravention or offence began` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 110(2) the old regulations continue to have effect` IS
    IF `the day the conduct constituting the contravention or offence began` < `reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the conduct ... began before the date on which these Regulations come into force" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]

-- Reg 110(3): where the old regulations continue to have effect, a penalty or an offence under the relevant Part of these Regulations is not to have effect in such circumstances.
-- src:2947 | (3) Where the old money laundering regulations or the old transfer of funds regulations continue to have effect, a penalty or an offence under the relevant Part of these Regulations is not to have effect in such circumstances.
@ref reg 110(3) (src:2947)
GIVEN `reg 110(2) the old regulations continue to have effect` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 110(3) a penalty or an offence under the relevant Part of these Regulations has effect` IS
    IF `reg 110(2) the old regulations continue to have effect` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a penalty or an offence under the relevant Part of these Regulations is not to have effect in such circumstances" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- Reg 110(4): where the conduct is found to have been committed over two or more days, or at some point during such a period, it is taken to have begun on the earliest of those days.
-- src:2948 | (4) Where the conduct is found to have been committed over a period of two or more days, or at some point during a period of two or more days, it is to be taken for the purposes of paragraph (2) to have been begun on the earliest of those days.
@ref reg 110(4) (src:2948)
GIVEN `the conduct is found to have been committed over a period of two or more days, or at some point during such a period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earliest of those days` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `reg 110(4) the conduct is taken to have begun on` IS
    IF `the conduct is found to have been committed over a period of two or more days, or at some point during such a period`
    THEN JUST `the earliest of those days`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the conduct is found to have been committed over a period of two or more days"
